## Verification

```bash
# 1. Apply with a symlink, job, and install command in dotfiles.conf
cly dotfiles -a
# → lock file created at ~/.local/share/cly/dotfiles/dotfiles.lock

# 2. Remove the symlink entry from dotfiles.conf, re-run
cly dotfiles
# → symlink auto-removed, prominent warning about install command if one was removed

# 3. Run status — removed symlink no longer tracked
cly dotfiles status

# 4. Run tests
go test ./modules/dotfiles/... -v
```

## Decisions (from user)

1. **Lock location**: system data dir — `~/.local/share/cly/dotfiles/dotfiles.lock`
2. **Op mappings**: auto-delete the destination file when entry is removed
3. **Install commands**: no warning on remove — only prompt user interactively at the moment of detection
4. **Interactive prompt**: when removed install commands are detected, pause and require the user to press Enter to continue. Bypassable with `--no-it` flag. Uses same `bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)` pattern as `modules/update/cmd.go:158`.
